I'm also able to reproduce the failure. The situation, as far as I can=20
see,is as follow:

The problem was reported in bug #160637[1]. The maintainer solution[2]=20
applied was patch the ebuild to check if epoll support was enabled in=20
the kernel.

Ebuild works just fine, detecting if the kernel has the epoll support=20
enabled[3] and adding the proper --enable-epoll in that case.

So if the kernel has support for it, the problem should be in a=20
different place, probably glibc or linux-headers. I found a test case[4]=20
you can run just compiling it.

Later, I'll reopen the bug and see if one of our toolchain ninjas can=20
give it a try.

As a workaround, you can disable the epoll support commenting out the=20
"myconf ..." line in the ebuild (not tested but should work).

Thanks for reporting,
Regards.

--=20
Jose Luis Rivero <yoswink@gentoo.org>
Gentoo/Doc Gentoo/Alpha


[1] http://bugs.gentoo.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D160637

[2]
-------------------
if kernel_is ge 2 6 && linux_chkconfig_present EPOLL ; then
	myconf=3D"${myconf} --enable-epoll"
fi
-------------------

[3] # grep 'CONFIG_EPOLL' /usr/src/linux/.config

[4] http://www.xmailserver.org/linux-patches/pipetest.c
